/-!
# Full-span recognition in the large-intersection branch

The literal radius, starred and orbit-span quotients carry their descended
SL3(2) actions and exact relative Z_alpha kernels. Sections proves the two
rank-one section assertions in (1)--(2). Seed proves (3) conditional on its
compatible incident frame and actual seed. Transport moves critical segments
onto the distinguished edge without changing their marked span quotient.

`source_spanRecognition` assembles clauses (1)--(5) from CommonFacts,
RadiusFacts and b = 4. Clause (4) uses the actual orbit-span displacement
estimate to obtain pointwise involution rank bounds and full first-actor
fixation of Y. Clause (5) supplies dimension six and the literal midpoint
seed. Conjugate-seed recognition then gives the marked orbit-span quotient
and converts the dimension equality into relative starred index 64.
The older conditional assembly remains available. The distinct passage
from the Z_alpha quotient to the U_alpha kernel stays with FirstFactor.

Source: Meierfrankenfeld--Stellmacher (1993), (4.6.12)(1)--(5), printed
pp.910--912.
-/
